In article <4657@ucsbcsl.ucsb.edu>
	maarrrk@ruapehu.Caltech.Edu ( Mark Alan Erickson) writes:

 >In feudal Japan many samurai were trained to swim and engage in combat
 >in full armor in deep water.

Since ninjas has been removed from NetHack, there should
be a slight confusion between ninjas and samurais.

Ninjas are spies or something in the dark-side of the
world, while samurais are warriors under the sun.  You
can say "I am a samurai," but can't say "I am a ninja."

	o It is Ninja that uses osaku(lock-pick).
	o It is Ninja that wears black suits made from
	  cloth (kuro-shouzoku), under which he wears a
	  chain-mail (kusari-katabira).
	o It is Ninja that is trained to swim, to hide
	  in water, or even to walk over water
	  (specialized water-walking boots are
	  needed---called mizugumo or something? I can't
	  recall).
	o It is Samurai that uses Murasame-blade (does
	  it exist in NetHack?).
	o It is Samurai that has two swords, a katana
	  and a short sword (wakizashi).
	o Ninjas are stealth, but I doubt Samurais are.
	o Ninjas are agile rather than strong, while
	  Samurais are strong rather than agile.

Female ninjas are called 'kunoichi'. (Because writing
three letters 'ku', 'no', and 'ichi' at the same place
gets the letter 'onna' (meaning woman).)  Kunoichis are
said to make full use of their sexual abilities.

How about Ninja's coming back?  I can't judge which is
better to give a character class to ninja, or to unify
it with rogue (or change rogue to ninja).  (Possibly,
add ninja as an @ monster!)

Anyway, ninja should be definitely separated from samurai.
